# 2. Introduction

## 2.1 Background

Large enterprises such as Nestlé operate complex global supply chains consisting of:

- Manufacturing plants
- Distribution centers
- Warehouses
- Transportation networks
- Customer delivery systems

Every customer order requires a critical decision:

> "Which warehouse should fulfill this order?"

Selecting the wrong warehouse may result in:

- Higher transportation cost
- Inventory imbalance
- Delivery delays
- Increased penalty cost
- Reduced customer satisfaction


Therefore, an intelligent optimization system is required to make efficient fulfillment decisions.

---

# 2.2 Distributed Order Management (DOM)

Distributed Order Management is a supply chain strategy that determines:

- Where inventory is available
- Which location should fulfill an order
- How orders should be allocated
- How business objectives can be optimized


DOM balances:

```
Customer Satisfaction
        +
Operational Efficiency
        +
Cost Reduction
```

